+"{\"value\":{\"mdx\":\"# FAQ\\n\\n## What is the difference between Deploy and Transaction?\\n\\nCasper has two transaction formats:\\n\\n- **Deploy** - the original format used in Casper 1.x. Still supported by all nodes.\\n- **TransactionV1** - introduced in Casper 2.0. More efficient, supports new features.\\n\\nUse `Transaction` (the SDK wrapper class) which holds either format. All builders produce `Transaction`.\\n\\nUse `putTransaction()` for `Transaction` and `putDeploy()` only for raw `Deploy` objects.\\n\\n## How do I check my account balance?\\n\\n```ts\\nconst result = await rpcClient.queryLatestBalance({\\n  mainPurseUnderPublicKey: publicKey.toHex(),\\n});\\nconsole.log(result.balance.toString()); // in motes\\n// 1 CSPR = 1,000,000,000 motes\\n```\\n\\n## Why do I get `AccountMigratedToEntity`?\\n\\nYour account was created on Casper 1.x and migrated during the Casper 2.0 upgrade. Use `getLatestEntity` instead of `getAccountInfo`:\\n\\n```ts\\nconst entity = await rpcClient.getLatestEntity({\\n  publicKey: publicKey.toHex(),\\n});\\n```\\n\\n## What is a mote?\\n\\nThe smallest unit of CSPR. `1 CSPR = 1,000,000,000 motes (10^9)`. All SDK amounts are in motes as strings to avoid floating point issues.\\n\\n## How do I call a smart contract?\\n\\n```ts\\nconst args = Args.fromMap({\\n  amount: CLValue.newCLUInt256('1000000000'),\\n  recipient: CLValue.newCLPublicKey(recipientKey),\\n});\\n\\nconst tx = new ContractCallBuilder()\\n  .from(senderPublicKey)\\n  .byHash('hash-contract-abc...')\\n  .entryPoint('transfer')\\n  .runtimeArgs(args)\\n  .chainName('casper')\\n  .payment(3_000_000_000)\\n  .build();\\n```\\n\\n## What is a URef?\\n\\nAn Unforgeable Reference - a capability token that grants access to a storage location (purse, dictionary, contract state). Format: `uref-{32-byte-hex}-{octal-access-rights}`.\\n\\n## Does the SDK work in the browser?\\n\\nYes. Use `dist/lib.web.js` or import from the package with a bundler. The `eventsource` package provides SSE support in environments without native `EventSource`.\\n\\n## How do I use hardware wallets?\\n\\nGet the bytes to sign, send them to the hardware wallet, then set the signature:\\n\\n```ts\\nconst tx = new NativeTransferBuilder()...build();\\nconst bytesToSign = tx.getTransactionV1()!.hash.toBytes();\\n// → send bytesToSign to hardware wallet\\nconst signature = await hardwareWallet.sign(bytesToSign);\\ntx.setSignature(signature, publicKey);\\n```\\n\",\"document\":[{\"href\":\"/docs/faq#faq\",\"html\":\"</header>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/faq.mdx#faq\",\"isPage\":true,\"text\":\"\\n\",\"title\":\"FAQ\",\"titles\":[]},{\"href\":\"/docs/faq#what-is-the-difference-between-deploy-and-transaction\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>Casper has two transaction formats:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Deploy</strong> - the original format used in Casper 1.x. Still supported by all nodes.</li>\\n<li><strong>TransactionV1</strong> - introduced in Casper 2.0. More efficient, supports new features.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>Use <code>Transaction</code> (the SDK wrapper class) which holds either format. All builders produce <code>Transaction</code>.</p>\\n<p>Use <code>putTransaction()</code> for <code>Transaction</code> and <code>putDeploy()</code> only for raw <code>Deploy</code> objects.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/faq.mdx#what-is-the-difference-between-deploy-and-transaction\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nCasper has two transaction formats:\\n\\nDeploy - the original format used in Casper 1.x. Still supported by all nodes.\\nTransactionV1 - introduced in Casper 2.0. More efficient, supports new features.\\n\\nUse Transaction (the SDK wrapper class) which holds either format. All builders produce Transaction.\\nUse putTransaction() for Transaction and putDeploy() only for raw Deploy objects.\\n\",\"title\":\"What is the difference between Deploy and Transaction?\",\"titles\":[\"FAQ\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/faq#how-do-i-check-my-account-balance\",\"html\":\"\\n<pre class=\\\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\\\" style=\\\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7\\\" tabindex=\\\"0\\\"><code><span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">const</span><span style=\\\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\\\"> result</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> =</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> await</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> rpcClient.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">queryLatestBalance</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">({</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  mainPurseUnderPublicKey: publicKey.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">toHex</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(),</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">});</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">console.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">log</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(result.balance.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">toString</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">()); </span><span style=\\\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\\\">// in motes</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\\\">// 1 CSPR = 1,000,000,000 motes</span></span></code></pre>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/faq.mdx#how-do-i-check-my-account-balance\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nconst result = await rpcClient.queryLatestBalance({\\n  mainPurseUnderPublicKey: publicKey.toHex(),\\n});\\nconsole.log(result.balance.toString()); // in motes\\n// 1 CSPR = 1,000,000,000 motes\\n\",\"title\":\"How do I check my account balance?\",\"titles\":[\"FAQ\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/faq#why-do-i-get-accountmigratedtoentity\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>Your account was created on Casper 1.x and migrated during the Casper 2.0 upgrade. Use <code>getLatestEntity</code> instead of <code>getAccountInfo</code>:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\\\" style=\\\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7\\\" tabindex=\\\"0\\\"><code><span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">const</span><span style=\\\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\\\"> entity</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> =</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> await</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> rpcClient.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">getLatestEntity</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">({</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  publicKey: publicKey.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">toHex</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(),</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">});</span></span></code></pre>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/faq.mdx#why-do-i-get-accountmigratedtoentity\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nYour account was created on Casper 1.x and migrated during the Casper 2.0 upgrade. Use getLatestEntity instead of getAccountInfo:\\nconst entity = await rpcClient.getLatestEntity({\\n  publicKey: publicKey.toHex(),\\n});\\n\",\"title\":\"Why do I get AccountMigratedToEntity?\",\"titles\":[\"FAQ\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/faq#what-is-a-mote\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The smallest unit of CSPR. <code>1 CSPR = 1,000,000,000 motes (10^9)</code>. All SDK amounts are in motes as strings to avoid floating point issues.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/faq.mdx#what-is-a-mote\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe smallest unit of CSPR. 1 CSPR = 1,000,000,000 motes (10^9). All SDK amounts are in motes as strings to avoid floating point issues.\\n\",\"title\":\"What is a mote?\",\"titles\":[\"FAQ\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/faq#how-do-i-call-a-smart-contract\",\"html\":\"\\n<pre class=\\\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\\\" style=\\\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7\\\" tabindex=\\\"0\\\"><code><span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">const</span><span style=\\\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\\\"> args</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> =</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> Args.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">fromMap</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">({</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  amount: CLValue.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">newCLUInt256</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(</span><span style=\\\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\\\">&#x27;1000000000&#x27;</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">),</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  recipient: CLValue.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">newCLPublicKey</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(recipientKey),</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">});</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\" data-empty-line=\\\"true\\\"> </span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">const</span><span style=\\\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\\\"> tx</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> =</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> new</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\"> ContractCallBuilder</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">()</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  .</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">from</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(senderPublicKey)</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  .</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">byHash</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(</span><span style=\\\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\\\">&#x27;hash-contract-abc...&#x27;</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">)</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  .</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">entryPoint</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(</span><span style=\\\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\\\">&#x27;transfer&#x27;</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">)</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  .</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">runtimeArgs</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(args)</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  .</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">chainName</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(</span><span style=\\\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\\\">&#x27;casper&#x27;</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">)</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  .</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">payment</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(</span><span style=\\\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\\\">3_000_000_000</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">)</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  .</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">build</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">();</span></span></code></pre>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/faq.mdx#how-do-i-call-a-smart-contract\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nconst args = Args.fromMap({\\n  amount: CLValue.newCLUInt256(&#x27;1000000000&#x27;),\\n  recipient: CLValue.newCLPublicKey(recipientKey),\\n});\\n \\nconst tx = new ContractCallBuilder()\\n  .from(senderPublicKey)\\n  .byHash(&#x27;hash-contract-abc...&#x27;)\\n  .entryPoint(&#x27;transfer&#x27;)\\n  .runtimeArgs(args)\\n  .chainName(&#x27;casper&#x27;)\\n  .payment(3_000_000_000)\\n  .build();\\n\",\"title\":\"How do I call a smart contract?\",\"titles\":[\"FAQ\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/faq#what-is-a-uref\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>An Unforgeable Reference - a capability token that grants access to a storage location (purse, dictionary, contract state). Format: <code>uref-{32-byte-hex}-{octal-access-rights}</code>.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/faq.mdx#what-is-a-uref\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nAn Unforgeable Reference - a capability token that grants access to a storage location (purse, dictionary, contract state). Format: uref-{32-byte-hex}-{octal-access-rights}.\\n\",\"title\":\"What is a URef?\",\"titles\":[\"FAQ\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/faq#does-the-sdk-work-in-the-browser\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>Yes. Use <code>dist/lib.web.js</code> or import from the package with a bundler. The <code>eventsource</code> package provides SSE support in environments without native <code>EventSource</code>.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/faq.mdx#does-the-sdk-work-in-the-browser\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nYes. Use dist/lib.web.js or import from the package with a bundler. The eventsource package provides SSE support in environments without native EventSource.\\n\",\"title\":\"Does the SDK work in the browser?\",\"titles\":[\"FAQ\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/faq#how-do-i-use-hardware-wallets\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>Get the bytes to sign, send them to the hardware wallet, then set the signature:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\\\" style=\\\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7\\\" tabindex=\\\"0\\\"><code><span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">const</span><span style=\\\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\\\"> tx</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> =</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> new</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\"> NativeTransferBuilder</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">()</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">...</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">build</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">();</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">const</span><span style=\\\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\\\"> bytesToSign</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> =</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> tx.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">getTransactionV1</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">()</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">!</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">.hash.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">toBytes</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">();</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\\\">// → send bytesToSign to hardware wallet</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">const</span><span style=\\\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\\\"> signature</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> =</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> await</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> hardwareWallet.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">sign</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(bytesToSign);</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">tx.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">setSignature</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(signature, publicKey);</span></span></code></pre>\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/faq.mdx#how-do-i-use-hardware-wallets\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nGet the bytes to sign, send them to the hardware wallet, then set the signature:\\nconst tx = new NativeTransferBuilder()...build();\\nconst bytesToSign = tx.getTransactionV1()!.hash.toBytes();\\n// → send bytesToSign to hardware wallet\\nconst signature = await hardwareWallet.sign(bytesToSign);\\ntx.setSignature(signature, publicKey);\",\"title\":\"How do I use hardware wallets?\",\"titles\":[\"FAQ\"]}]}}"
