+"{\"value\":{\"mdx\":\"# getAccountInfo\\n\\nReturns the account information for a public key (Casper 1.x format).\\n\\n## Import\\n\\n```ts\\nimport { RpcClient, HttpHandler, PublicKey } from 'casper-js-sdk';\\n```\\n\\n## Usage\\n\\n```ts\\nconst result = await rpcClient.getAccountInfo('latest', publicKey);\\n\\nconsole.log(result.account.accountHash().toFormattedStr());\\nconsole.log(result.account.mainPurse); // URef string\\n```\\n\\n## Parameters\\n\\n### blockHash\\n\\n- **Type:** `string`\\n\\nThe block hash to query at. Use `'latest'` for the current state.\\n\\n### publicKey\\n\\n- **Type:** `PublicKey`\\n\\nThe public key to look up.\\n\\n## Return Value\\n\\n`Promise<StateGetAccountInfoResult>`\\n\\n```ts\\ninterface StateGetAccountInfoResult {\\n  account: AccountInfo;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n:::warning\\nOn Casper 2.0 nodes, accounts created before the Casper 2.0 upgrade may have been migrated. This method will throw `RpcError` with `ErrorCode.AccountMigratedToEntity`. Use [`getLatestEntity`](/actions/account/getLatestEntity) as a fallback.\\n:::\\n\\n## Version-Compatible Pattern\\n\\n```ts\\nimport { RpcError, ErrorCode } from 'casper-js-sdk';\\n\\nasync function getAccount(publicKey: PublicKey) {\\n  try {\\n    return await rpcClient.getAccountInfo('latest', publicKey);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    if (err instanceof RpcError && err.code === ErrorCode.AccountMigratedToEntity) {\\n      return await rpcClient.getLatestEntity({ publicKey: publicKey.toHex() });\\n    }\\n    throw err;\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- [`getLatestEntity`](/actions/account/getLatestEntity)\\n\",\"document\":[{\"href\":\"/actions/account/getAccountInfo#getaccountinfo\",\"html\":\"</header>\\n<p>Returns the account information for a public key (Casper 1.x format).</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/actions/account/getAccountInfo.mdx#getaccountinfo\",\"isPage\":true,\"text\":\"\\nReturns the account information for a public key (Casper 1.x format).\\n\",\"title\":\"getAccountInfo\",\"titl