+"{\"value\":{\"mdx\":\"# Why Casper JS SDK\\n\\n<img src=\\\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/668fef77d8ac075ed5e3f57a/66900f439d0597692b64fcf2_Casper_Wordmark_Red_RGB.png\\\" alt=\\\"Casper Network\\\" style={{ height: '36px', marginBottom: '16px' }} />\\n\\nThe Casper JS SDK is the official TypeScript/JavaScript library for building applications on the [Casper Network](https://casper.network). It provides a complete, type-safe interface for key management, transaction construction, node queries, and real-time event streaming.\\n\\n## Motivation\\n\\nThe Casper blockchain has a unique architecture - two coexisting transaction formats (legacy `Deploy` for 1.x and `TransactionV1` for Casper 2.0), a contract-language value system (CLValues) for all smart contract interactions, and a bytesrepr binary serialization format for hashing and signing.\\n\\nThe SDK handles all of this complexity so you don't have to:\\n\\n- **No manual serialization** - every type implements `toBytes()` and `toJSON()` correctly\\n- **No format guessing** - `CasperNetwork.create()` detects the node version and dispatches automatically\\n- **No boilerplate** - fluent transaction builders handle all required fields\\n\\n## Design Principles\\n\\n### Type Safety\\nEvery public API is fully typed. RPC responses, CLValues, transaction fields - everything is a TypeScript type, not `any`.\\n\\n### Dual Transaction Support\\nCasper 2.0 introduced `TransactionV1`. The SDK fully supports both formats and provides version-aware utilities.\\n\\n### Minimal Dependencies\\nCore cryptography uses `@noble/curves`, `@noble/ed25519`, and `@noble/hashes` - audited, dependency-free implementations.\\n\\n## Comparison\\n\\n| Feature | casper-js-sdk v5 |\\n|---|---|\\n| TypeScript | ✅ Full types |\\n| TransactionV1 | ✅ Builders + bytesrepr |\\n| Legacy Deploy | ✅ Full support |\\n| CLValues | ✅ Complete type system |\\n| SSE streaming | ✅ All event types |\\n| Browser + Node.js | ✅ Dual bundles |\\n| Version auto-detection | ✅ CasperNetwork |\\n| ED25519 + SECP256K1 | ✅ Both algorithms |\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n\\n- [Getting Started](/docs/getting-started) - install and run your first transfer\\n- [Clients](/clients/intro) - understand RpcClient and SseClient\\n- [Transaction Builders](/builders/introduction) - build and sign transactions\\n\",\"document\":[{\"href\":\"/docs/introduction#why-casper-js-sdk\",\"html\":\"</header>\\n<img src=\\\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/668fef77d8ac075ed5e3f57a/66900f439d0597692b64fcf2_Casper_Wordmark_Red_RGB.png\\\" alt=\\\"Casper Network\\\" style=\\\"height:36px;margin-bottom:16px\\\"/>\\n<p>The Casper JS SDK is the official TypeScript/JavaScript library for building applications on the <a href=\\\"https://casper.network\\\">Casper Network</a>. It provides a complete, type-safe interface for key management, transaction construction, node queries, and real-time event streaming.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/introduction.mdx#why-casper-js-sdk\",\"isPage\":true,\"text\":\"\\n\\nThe Casper JS SDK is the official TypeScript/JavaScript library for building applications on the Casper Network. It provides a complete, type-safe interface for key management, transaction construction, node queries, and real-time event streaming.\\n\",\"title\":\"Why Casper JS SDK\",\"titles\":[]},{\"href\":\"/docs/introduction#motivation\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The Casper blockchain has a unique architecture - two coexisting transaction formats (legacy <code>Deploy</code> for 1.x and <code>TransactionV1</code> for Casper 2.0), a contract-language value system (CLValues) for all smart contract interactions, and a bytesrepr binary serialization format for hashing and signing.</p>\\n<p>The SDK handles all of this complexity so you don&#x27;t have to:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>No manual serialization</strong> - every type implements <code>toBytes()</code> and <code>toJSON()</code> correctly</li>\\n<li><strong>No format guessing</strong> - <code>CasperNetwork.create()</code> detects the node version and dispatches automatically</li>\\n<li><strong>No boilerplate</strong> - fluent transaction builders handle all required fields</li>\\n</ul>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/introduction.mdx#motivation\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe Casper blockchain has a unique architecture - two coexisting transaction formats (legacy Deploy for 1.x and TransactionV1 for Casper 2.0), a contract-language value system (CLValues) for all smart contract interactions, and a bytesrepr binary serialization format for hashing and signing.\\nThe SDK handles all of this complexity so you don&#x27;t have to:\\n\\nNo manual serialization - every type implements toBytes() and toJSON() correctly\\nNo format guessing - CasperNetwork.create() detects the node version and dispatches automatically\\nNo boilerplate - fluent transaction builders handle all required fields\\n\\n\",\"title\":\"Motivation\",\"titles\":[\"Why Casper JS SDK\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/introduction#design-principles\",\"html\":\"\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/introduction.mdx#design-principles\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\n\",\"title\":\"Design Principles\",\"titles\":[\"Why Casper JS SDK\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/introduction#type-safety\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>Every public API is fully typed. RPC responses, CLValues, transaction fields - everything is a TypeScript type, not <code>any</code>.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/introduction.mdx#type-safety\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nEvery public API is fully typed. RPC responses, CLValues, transaction fields - everything is a TypeScript type, not any.\\n\",\"title\":\"Type Safety\",\"titles\":[\"Why Casper JS SDK\",\"Design Principles\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/introduction#dual-transaction-support\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>Casper 2.0 introduced <code>TransactionV1</code>. The SDK fully supports both formats and provides version-aware utilities.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/introduction.mdx#dual-transaction-support\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nCasper 2.0 introduced TransactionV1. The SDK fully supports both formats and provides version-aware utilities.\\n\",\"title\":\"Dual Transaction Support\",\"titles\":[\"Why Casper JS SDK\",\"Design Principles\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/introduction#minimal-dependencies\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>Core cryptography uses <code>@noble/curves</code>, <code>@noble/ed25519</code>, and <code>@noble/hashes</code> - audited, dependency-free implementations.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/introduction.mdx#minimal-dependencies\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nCore cryptography uses @noble/curves, @noble/ed25519, and @noble/hashes - audited, dependency-free implementations.\\n\",\"title\":\"Minimal Dependencies\",\"titles\":[\"Why Casper JS SDK\",\"Design Principles\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/introduction#comparison\",\"html\":\"\\n<table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>casper-js-sdk v5</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>TypeScript</td><td>✅ Full types</td></tr><tr><td>TransactionV1</td><td>✅ Builders + bytesrepr</td></tr><tr><td>Legacy Deploy</td><td>✅ Full support</td></tr><tr><td>CLValues</td><td>✅ Complete type system</td></tr><tr><td>SSE streaming</td><td>✅ All event types</td></tr><tr><td>Browser + Node.js</td><td>✅ Dual bundles</td></tr><tr><td>Version auto-detection</td><td>✅ CasperNetwork</td></tr><tr><td>ED25519 + SECP256K1</td><td>✅ Both algorithms</td></tr></tbody></table>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/introduction.mdx#comparison\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nFeaturecasper-js-sdk v5TypeScript✅ Full typesTransactionV1✅ Builders + bytesreprLegacy Deploy✅ Full supportCLValues✅ Complete type systemSSE streaming✅ All event typesBrowser + Node.js✅ Dual bundlesVersion auto-detection✅ CasperNetworkED25519 + SECP256K1✅ Both algorithms\\n\",\"title\":\"Comparison\",\"titles\":[\"Why Casper JS SDK\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/introduction#next-steps\",\"html\":\"\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"/docs/getting-started\\\">Getting Started</a> - install and run your first transfer</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"/clients/intro\\\">Clients</a> - understand RpcClient and SseClient</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"/builders/introduction\\\">Transaction Builders</a> - build and sign transactions</li>\\n</ul>\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/introduction.mdx#next-steps\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\n\\nGetting Started - install and run your first transfer\\nClients - understand RpcClient and SseClient\\nTransaction Builders - build and sign transactions\\n\",\"title\":\"Next Steps\",\"titles\":[\"Why Casper JS SDK\"]}]}}"
