+"{\"value\":{\"mdx\":\"# Terms\\n\\nGlossary of Casper Network and SDK terminology.\\n\\n## Mote\\n\\nThe smallest unit of CSPR (the Casper native token).\\n\\n`1 CSPR = 1,000,000,000 motes (10^9)`\\n\\nAll SDK amount fields use motes as strings to avoid floating-point issues.\\n\\n## Deploy\\n\\nThe original Casper transaction format (1.x). Still supported on all nodes. Replaced by `TransactionV1` in Casper 2.x.\\n\\n## TransactionV1\\n\\nThe modern Casper transaction format introduced in the Casper 2.0 upgrade. More efficient, supports new pricing modes and entry point types.\\n\\n## Transaction\\n\\nThe SDK's unified wrapper class over both `Deploy` and `TransactionV1`. Use `Transaction.getDeploy()` or `Transaction.getTransactionV1()` to access the specific format.\\n\\n## Era\\n\\nThe time unit for consensus in Casper. Each era is approximately 2 hours on mainnet. Validator weights and rewards are distributed per era.\\n\\n## Account Hash\\n\\nThe on-chain identifier for an account. Derived as `blake2b-256(\\\"ed25519\\\\0\\\" + publicKeyBytes)` (or `\\\"secp256k1\\\\0\\\"` for SECP256K1). Format: `account-hash-{64-hex-chars}`.\\n\\n## URef (Unforgeable Reference)\\n\\nA capability token granting access to a storage location. Format: `uref-{64-hex}-{3-octal}`. The octal suffix encodes access rights (read, write, add).\\n\\n## CLValue\\n\\nA typed value in Casper's Contract Language (CL) type system. Every smart contract argument and return value is a CLValue.\\n\\n## CLType\\n\\nThe type descriptor for a CLValue. Primitive types: Bool, I32, I64, U8, U32, U64, U128, U256, U512, String, Key, URef, PublicKey, Any. Parameterized: List, Map, Option, Result, Tuple1/2/3, ByteArray.\\n\\n## AccountHash\\n\\nThe 32-byte on-chain account identifier derived from a public key via blake2b-256.\\n\\n## AddressableEntity\\n\\nThe Casper 2.0 concept that generalizes accounts and contracts into a single addressable entity type.\\n\\n## BidAddr\\n\\nA validator bid address type introduced in Casper 2.x for the new auction system. Variants: Validator, Delegator, Credit, UnifiedBid.\\n\\n## Casper 2.0\\n\\nThe Casper 2.0 protocol upgrade. Introduced TransactionV1, AddressableEntity, new auction mechanics, and improved pricing.\\n\\n## Bytesrepr\\n\\nThe Casper binary serialization format. Used for computing hashes and signing. Little-endian integers, length-prefixed strings and collections.\\n\\n## State Root Hash\\n\\nA Merkle root over all on-chain state at a given block. Used as a stable reference point for state queries.\\n\\n## EntryPoint\\n\\nA named callable function in a Casper smart contract. Called via `ContractCallBuilder.entryPoint(name)`.\\n\",\"document\":[{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#terms\",\"html\":\"</header>\\n<p>Glossary of Casper Network and SDK terminology.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#terms\",\"isPage\":true,\"text\":\"\\nGlossary of Casper Network and SDK terminology.\\n\",\"title\":\"Terms\",\"titles\":[]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#mote\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The smallest unit of CSPR (the Casper native token).</p>\\n<p><code>1 CSPR = 1,000,000,000 motes (10^9)</code></p>\\n<p>All SDK amount fields use motes as strings to avoid floating-point issues.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#mote\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe smallest unit of CSPR (the Casper native token).\\n1 CSPR = 1,000,000,000 motes (10^9)\\nAll SDK amount fields use motes as strings to avoid floating-point issues.\\n\",\"title\":\"Mote\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#deploy\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The original Casper transaction format (1.x). Still supported on all nodes. Replaced by <code>TransactionV1</code> in Casper 2.x.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#deploy\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe original Casper transaction format (1.x). Still supported on all nodes. Replaced by TransactionV1 in Casper 2.x.\\n\",\"title\":\"Deploy\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#transactionv1\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The modern Casper transaction format introduced in the Casper 2.0 upgrade. More efficient, supports new pricing modes and entry point types.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#transactionv1\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe modern Casper transaction format introduced in the Casper 2.0 upgrade. More efficient, supports new pricing modes and entry point types.\\n\",\"title\":\"TransactionV1\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#transaction\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The SDK&#x27;s unified wrapper class over both <code>Deploy</code> and <code>TransactionV1</code>. Use <code>Transaction.getDeploy()</code> or <code>Transaction.getTransactionV1()</code> to access the specific format.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#transaction\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe SDK&#x27;s unified wrapper class over both Deploy and TransactionV1. Use Transaction.getDeploy() or Transaction.getTransactionV1() to access the specific format.\\n\",\"title\":\"Transaction\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#era\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The time unit for consensus in Casper. Each era is approximately 2 hours on mainnet. Validator weights and rewards are distributed per era.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#era\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe time unit for consensus in Casper. Each era is approximately 2 hours on mainnet. Validator weights and rewards are distributed per era.\\n\",\"title\":\"Era\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#account-hash\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The on-chain identifier for an account. Derived as <code>blake2b-256(&quot;ed25519\\\\0&quot; + publicKeyBytes)</code> (or <code>&quot;secp256k1\\\\0&quot;</code> for SECP256K1). Format: <code>account-hash-{64-hex-chars}</code>.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#account-hash\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe on-chain identifier for an account. Derived as blake2b-256(&quot;ed25519\\\\0&quot; + publicKeyBytes) (or &quot;secp256k1\\\\0&quot; for SECP256K1). Format: account-hash-{64-hex-chars}.\\n\",\"title\":\"Account Hash\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#uref-unforgeable-reference\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>A capability token granting access to a storage location. Format: <code>uref-{64-hex}-{3-octal}</code>. The octal suffix encodes access rights (read, write, add).</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#uref-unforgeable-reference\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nA capability token granting access to a storage location. Format: uref-{64-hex}-{3-octal}. The octal suffix encodes access rights (read, write, add).\\n\",\"title\":\"URef (Unforgeable Reference)\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#clvalue\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>A typed value in Casper&#x27;s Contract Language (CL) type system. Every smart contract argument and return value is a CLValue.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#clvalue\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nA typed value in Casper&#x27;s Contract Language (CL) type system. Every smart contract argument and return value is a CLValue.\\n\",\"title\":\"CLValue\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#cltype\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The type descriptor for a CLValue. Primitive types: Bool, I32, I64, U8, U32, U64, U128, U256, U512, String, Key, URef, PublicKey, Any. Parameterized: List, Map, Option, Result, Tuple1/2/3, ByteArray.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#cltype\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe type descriptor for a CLValue. Primitive types: Bool, I32, I64, U8, U32, U64, U128, U256, U512, String, Key, URef, PublicKey, Any. Parameterized: List, Map, Option, Result, Tuple1/2/3, ByteArray.\\n\",\"title\":\"CLType\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#accounthash\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The 32-byte on-chain account identifier derived from a public key via blake2b-256.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#accounthash\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe 32-byte on-chain account identifier derived from a public key via blake2b-256.\\n\",\"title\":\"AccountHash\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#addressableentity\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The Casper 2.0 concept that generalizes accounts and contracts into a single addressable entity type.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#addressableentity\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe Casper 2.0 concept that generalizes accounts and contracts into a single addressable entity type.\\n\",\"title\":\"AddressableEntity\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#bidaddr\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>A validator bid address type introduced in Casper 2.x for the new auction system. Variants: Validator, Delegator, Credit, UnifiedBid.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#bidaddr\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nA validator bid address type introduced in Casper 2.x for the new auction system. Variants: Validator, Delegator, Credit, UnifiedBid.\\n\",\"title\":\"BidAddr\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#casper-20\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The Casper 2.0 protocol upgrade. Introduced TransactionV1, AddressableEntity, new auction mechanics, and improved pricing.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#casper-20\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe Casper 2.0 protocol upgrade. Introduced TransactionV1, AddressableEntity, new auction mechanics, and improved pricing.\\n\",\"title\":\"Casper 2.0\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#bytesrepr\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The Casper binary serialization format. Used for computing hashes and signing. Little-endian integers, length-prefixed strings and collections.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#bytesrepr\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe Casper binary serialization format. Used for computing hashes and signing. Little-endian integers, length-prefixed strings and collections.\\n\",\"title\":\"Bytesrepr\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#state-root-hash\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>A Merkle root over all on-chain state at a given block. Used as a stable reference point for state queries.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#state-root-hash\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nA Merkle root over all on-chain state at a given block. Used as a stable reference point for state queries.\\n\",\"title\":\"State Root Hash\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]},{\"href\":\"/glossary/terms#entrypoint\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>A named callable function in a Casper smart contract. Called via <code>ContractCallBuilder.entryPoint(name)</code>.</p>\",\"id\":\"pages/glossary/terms.mdx#entrypoint\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nA named callable function in a Casper smart contract. Called via ContractCallBuilder.entryPoint(name).\",\"title\":\"EntryPoint\",\"titles\":[\"Terms\"]}]}}"
