+"{\"value\":{\"mdx\":\"# Error Handling\\n\\nThe SDK uses several error patterns depending on the layer.\\n\\n## RpcError\\n\\nThrown when the Casper node returns a JSON-RPC error response.\\n\\n```ts\\nimport { RpcError, ErrorCode } from 'casper-js-sdk';\\n\\ntry {\\n  await rpcClient.queryLatestBalance({\\n    mainPurseUnderPublicKey: publicKey.toHex(),\\n  });\\n} catch (err) {\\n  if (err instanceof RpcError) {\\n    console.log(err.code);    // ErrorCode number\\n    console.log(err.message); // Error description\\n    console.log(err.data);    // Optional additional data\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### ErrorCode\\n\\n| Constant | Value | When |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `NoSuchEntity` | -32001 | Account or entity not found |\\n| `AccountMigratedToEntity` | -32002 | 1.x account migrated to 2.x entity |\\n| `NoSuchBlock` | -32003 | Block hash/height not found |\\n| `NoSuchDeploy` | -32004 | Deploy or transaction hash not found |\\n| `FailedToGetBalance` | -32005 | Balance query failed |\\n\\n### Version-Compatible Account Query\\n\\nThe `AccountMigratedToEntity` error is common when querying accounts on Casper 2.0 nodes using the old `getAccountInfo` method:\\n\\n```ts\\nimport { RpcError, ErrorCode } from 'casper-js-sdk';\\n\\nasync function getAccount(publicKey: PublicKey) {\\n  try {\\n    return await rpcClient.getAccountInfo('latest', publicKey);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    if (err instanceof RpcError && err.code === ErrorCode.AccountMigratedToEntity) {\\n      // Account migrated to Casper 2.0 entity - use the new API\\n      return await rpcClient.getLatestEntity({ publicKey: publicKey.toHex() });\\n    }\\n    throw err;\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## HttpError\\n\\nThrown for HTTP transport failures (network errors, non-200 responses).\\n\\n```ts\\nimport { HttpError } from 'casper-js-sdk';\\n\\ntry {\\n  await rpcClient.getStatus();\\n} catch (err) {\\n  if (err instanceof HttpError) {\\n    console.log(err.statusCode); // HTTP status code\\n    console.log(err.message);\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## SSE Result Errors\\n\\nThe SSE client uses `ts-results` `Result<T, string>` for subscribe/unsubscribe:\\n\\n```ts\\nconst result = sseClient.subscribe(EventName.BlockAddedEventType, handler);\\nif (result.err) {\\n  // result.val is the error string\\n  console.error('Subscribe failed:', result.val);\\n}\\n```\\n\\nCommon SSE error strings:\\n- `'Already subscribed to this event'` - duplicate subscribe\\n- `'Not subscribed to this event'` - unsubscribe when not subscribed\\n\\n## Custom Error Classes\\n\\nSome modules throw typed errors for invalid inputs:\\n\\n- `ErrInvalidPublicKeyAlgo` - unknown key algorithm\\n- `ErrInvalidBidAddrTag` - malformed BidAddr tag byte\\n\\nThese are thrown synchronously during construction, not during network calls.\\n\",\"document\":[{\"href\":\"/docs/error-handling#error-handling\",\"html\":\"</header>\\n<p>The SDK uses several error patterns depending on the layer.</p>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/error-handling.mdx#error-handling\",\"isPage\":true,\"text\":\"\\nThe SDK uses several error patterns depending on the layer.\\n\",\"title\":\"Error Handling\",\"titles\":[]},{\"href\":\"/docs/error-handling#rpcerror\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>Thrown when the Casper node returns a JSON-RPC error response.</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\\\" style=\\\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7\\\" tabindex=\\\"0\\\"><code><span class=\\\"line\\\" data-empty-line=\\\"true\\\"> </span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\" data-empty-line=\\\"true\\\"> </span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">try</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> {</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">  await</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> rpcClient.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">queryLatestBalance</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">({</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">    mainPurseUnderPublicKey: publicKey.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">toHex</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(),</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  });</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">} </span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">catch</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> (err) {</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">  if</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> (err </span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">instanceof</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\\\"> RpcError</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">) {</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">    console.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">log</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(err.code);    </span><span style=\\\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\\\">// ErrorCode number</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">    console.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">log</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(err.message); </span><span style=\\\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\\\">// Error description</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">    console.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">log</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(err.data);    </span><span style=\\\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\\\">// Optional additional data</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  }</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">}</span></span></code></pre>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/error-handling.mdx#rpcerror\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThrown when the Casper node returns a JSON-RPC error response.\\n \\n \\ntry {\\n  await rpcClient.queryLatestBalance({\\n    mainPurseUnderPublicKey: publicKey.toHex(),\\n  });\\n} catch (err) {\\n  if (err instanceof RpcError) {\\n    console.log(err.code);    // ErrorCode number\\n    console.log(err.message); // Error description\\n    console.log(err.data);    // Optional additional data\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"title\":\"RpcError\",\"titles\":[\"Error Handling\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/error-handling#errorcode\",\"html\":\"\\n<table><thead><tr><th>Constant</th><th>Value</th><th>When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>NoSuchEntity</code></td><td>-32001</td><td>Account or entity not found</td></tr><tr><td><code>AccountMigratedToEntity</code></td><td>-32002</td><td>1.x account migrated to 2.x entity</td></tr><tr><td><code>NoSuchBlock</code></td><td>-32003</td><td>Block hash/height not found</td></tr><tr><td><code>NoSuchDeploy</code></td><td>-32004</td><td>Deploy or transaction hash not found</td></tr><tr><td><code>FailedToGetBalance</code></td><td>-32005</td><td>Balance query failed</td></tr></tbody></table>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/error-handling.mdx#errorcode\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nConstantValueWhenNoSuchEntity-32001Account or entity not foundAccountMigratedToEntity-320021.x account migrated to 2.x entityNoSuchBlock-32003Block hash/height not foundNoSuchDeploy-32004Deploy or transaction hash not foundFailedToGetBalance-32005Balance query failed\\n\",\"title\":\"ErrorCode\",\"titles\":[\"Error Handling\",\"RpcError\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/error-handling#version-compatible-account-query\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The <code>AccountMigratedToEntity</code> error is common when querying accounts on Casper 2.0 nodes using the old <code>getAccountInfo</code> method:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\\\" style=\\\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7\\\" tabindex=\\\"0\\\"><code><span class=\\\"line\\\" data-empty-line=\\\"true\\\"> </span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\" data-empty-line=\\\"true\\\"> </span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">async</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> function</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\"> getAccount</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(</span><span style=\\\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\\\">publicKey</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">:</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\\\"> PublicKey</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">) {</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">  try</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> {</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">    return</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> await</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> rpcClient.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">getAccountInfo</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(</span><span style=\\\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\\\">&#x27;latest&#x27;</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">, publicKey);</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  } </span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">catch</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> (err) {</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">    if</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> (err </span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">instanceof</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\\\"> RpcError</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> &amp;&amp;</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> err.code </span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">===</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> ErrorCode.AccountMigratedToEntity) {</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\\\">      // Account migrated to Casper 2.0 entity - use the new API</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">      return</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> await</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> rpcClient.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">getLatestEntity</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">({ publicKey: publicKey.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">toHex</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">() });</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">    }</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">    throw</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> err;</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  }</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">}</span></span></code></pre>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/error-handling.mdx#version-compatible-account-query\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe AccountMigratedToEntity error is common when querying accounts on Casper 2.0 nodes using the old getAccountInfo method:\\n \\n \\nasync function getAccount(publicKey: PublicKey) {\\n  try {\\n    return await rpcClient.getAccountInfo(&#x27;latest&#x27;, publicKey);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    if (err instanceof RpcError &amp;&amp; err.code === ErrorCode.AccountMigratedToEntity) {\\n      // Account migrated to Casper 2.0 entity - use the new API\\n      return await rpcClient.getLatestEntity({ publicKey: publicKey.toHex() });\\n    }\\n    throw err;\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"title\":\"Version-Compatible Account Query\",\"titles\":[\"Error Handling\",\"RpcError\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/error-handling#httperror\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>Thrown for HTTP transport failures (network errors, non-200 responses).</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\\\" style=\\\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7\\\" tabindex=\\\"0\\\"><code><span class=\\\"line\\\" data-empty-line=\\\"true\\\"> </span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\" data-empty-line=\\\"true\\\"> </span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">try</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> {</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">  await</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> rpcClient.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">getStatus</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">();</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">} </span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">catch</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> (err) {</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">  if</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> (err </span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">instanceof</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\\\"> HttpError</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">) {</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">    console.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">log</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(err.statusCode); </span><span style=\\\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\\\">// HTTP status code</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">    console.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">log</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(err.message);</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  }</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">}</span></span></code></pre>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/error-handling.mdx#httperror\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThrown for HTTP transport failures (network errors, non-200 responses).\\n \\n \\ntry {\\n  await rpcClient.getStatus();\\n} catch (err) {\\n  if (err instanceof HttpError) {\\n    console.log(err.statusCode); // HTTP status code\\n    console.log(err.message);\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"title\":\"HttpError\",\"titles\":[\"Error Handling\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/error-handling#sse-result-errors\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>The SSE client uses <code>ts-results</code> <code>Result</code> for subscribe/unsubscribe:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\\\" style=\\\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7\\\" tabindex=\\\"0\\\"><code><span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">const</span><span style=\\\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\\\"> result</span><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\"> =</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> sseClient.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">subscribe</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(EventName.BlockAddedEventType, handler);</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\\\">if</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\"> (result.err) {</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\\\">  // result.val is the error string</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">  console.</span><span style=\\\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\\\">error</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">(</span><span style=\\\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\\\">&#x27;Subscribe failed:&#x27;</span><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">, result.val);</span></span>\\n<span class=\\\"line\\\"><span style=\\\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\\\">}</span></span></code></pre>\\n<p>Common SSE error strings:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><code>&#x27;Already subscribed to this event&#x27;</code> - duplicate subscribe</li>\\n<li><code>&#x27;Not subscribed to this event&#x27;</code> - unsubscribe when not subscribed</li>\\n</ul>\\n\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/error-handling.mdx#sse-result-errors\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nThe SSE client uses ts-results Result for subscribe/unsubscribe:\\nconst result = sseClient.subscribe(EventName.BlockAddedEventType, handler);\\nif (result.err) {\\n  // result.val is the error string\\n  console.error(&#x27;Subscribe failed:&#x27;, result.val);\\n}\\nCommon SSE error strings:\\n\\n&#x27;Already subscribed to this event&#x27; - duplicate subscribe\\n&#x27;Not subscribed to this event&#x27; - unsubscribe when not subscribed\\n\\n\",\"title\":\"SSE Result Errors\",\"titles\":[\"Error Handling\"]},{\"href\":\"/docs/error-handling#custom-error-classes\",\"html\":\"\\n<p>Some modules throw typed errors for invalid inputs:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><code>ErrInvalidPublicKeyAlgo</code> - unknown key algorithm</li>\\n<li><code>ErrInvalidBidAddrTag</code> - malformed BidAddr tag byte</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>These are thrown synchronously during construction, not during network calls.</p>\",\"id\":\"pages/docs/error-handling.mdx#custom-error-classes\",\"isPage\":false,\"text\":\"\\nSome modules throw typed errors for invalid inputs:\\n\\nErrInvalidPublicKeyAlgo - unknown key algorithm\\nErrInvalidBidAddrTag - malformed BidAddr tag byte\\n\\nThese are thrown synchronously during construction, not during network calls.\",\"title\":\"Custom Error Classes\",\"titles\":[\"Error Handling\"]}]}}"
